              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp\u003EThe ClerksWell Charity Hackathon is happening on 28th November in London \n\nIf you can get to London on that day, please sign up to our free event\n\nhttps://clerkswell.com/hackathon25\n\nFAQs\n \n\u0026#127379; Is it free to enter?\nYes the hackathon is completely free to enter, you just need to make your way to London for the day. Food and drink will also be provided. If you live outside of London and travel costs are preventing you from attending please get in touch as we may be able to help you.\n \n\u0026#127942; What are the prizes?\nThere will be two winning teams, one for each of the two charity challenges.\nEach team will consist of 2 people.\nThe prize for each winning team is:\n1 Codegarden ticket\n1 Expert Training \u0026amp; Certification bundle\nIf your team wins, you\u2019ll need to decide between yourselves who gets which prize.\n \n\u0026#128187; How much Umbraco do we need to use?\nThere are no strict limits, just make sure you use Umbraco 17 in some way. It doesn\u2019t need to be a full-blown implementation. Be creative!\n \n\u23F1 What if we can\u0026#39;t finish a working solution in time?\nThat\u2019s totally fine. The judges will assess entries based on several criteria, including usability and how well the idea meets the brief. Even if your solution isn\u2019t fully working, your concept and approach still count.\n \n\u0026#128101; Do I need to already have a teammate?\nNo. We\u2019ve shared a private Slack channel with attendees where you can find a partner and form a team.\n \n\u0026#129504; How good do I need to be at coding?\nYou don\u2019t need to be an expert. If you team up with someone whose skills complement yours, you\u2019ll be in a great position. For example, if you\u0026#39;re stronger in front-end or UX, you could pair with someone who\u2019s more backend-focused.\nThere will also be people around to help if you get stuck.\n \n\u0026#128338; What are the timings? What if I arrive late or leave early?\nCoding starts at 10:00 and ends at 16:00.\nIf travel is a challenge, it\u2019s okay to arrive a bit late or leave slightly early. Just make sure you\u2019ve coordinated with your teammate in advance so you\u2019re aligned on what you\u2019ll be working on.\n \n\u0026#127760; Can I attend online?\nThis is an in-person event only.\nHowever, the challenge briefs are public, and you\u2019re welcome to try them out on your own. If you\u2019d like to share your work with the charities afterwards, we\u2019d be happy to connect you.\n \n\u0026#129777; Can I take part if I already know the charities or ClerksWell?\nYes, that\u2019s not a problem. There are six independent judges, and ClerksWell won\u2019t be involved in judging, to keep things fair.\n \n\u2764\uFE0F Are the charities connected to ClerksWell?\nThe charities are not clients of ClerksWell, but they are close to our hearts:\nHeadway was suggested by Paul, who previously worked at an agency that built their website. Several of Paul\u2019s family members have experienced brain injuries and benefited from Headway\u2019s services.\nRestore Hope was suggested by Marc from ClerksWell, who has volunteered with them and admires the work they do in his local area.\n\nLet me know if you have any others to add or want to change any. We are checking with Lotte about the one which mentions help with travel, so please don\u0026#39;t publish yet.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003E\u003Ca href=\u0022https://www.youtube.com/shorts/i5MIxUMbxwI\u0022 target=\u0022_blank\u0022 rel=\u0022noopener\u0022\u003ERead the original article\u003C/a\u003E\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
